### ns2d — CORRECTION superseding the §A11 wording in the 2026-09-17 ns304 entry: the "solve layer 4–10× above the manifold" compared two different statistics; on a matched statistic it is 1.4–2.5× (DESIGN §A14)

The ns304 entry above (and DESIGN §A11) divided the ROM's median-over-cases worst-evolved error by the manifold's median over all 48 states including t=0; the t=0 compression made the denominator too small. Found by the coordinator's read-only investigation of ns304 (`scratchpad/ns-invest/solve/report.md`); verified here independently from the archived per-state arrays. Corrected (median over cases of the worst evolved time on both sides): solved/manifold = **2.51 / 2.31 / 2.20 / 1.91 / 2.04 / 1.40** at q = 0/32/64/128/256/512 (was quoted as 3.9 … 10.8); solved/bank 23.7 → 1.40. Generated mechanism rows added: the per-time ratio grows along the trajectory (q=0: 1.44 → 3.85 at t=0.2…1); enstrophy ratio at t=1 median 1.043 (worst 1.119) at q=0, ≈1 at q=32, a deficit 0.95–0.97 at q=64–256, 0.999 at q=512; POD-32 control 1.026 (worst 1.158). The investigation's same-solver linear-control ratios (POD-32 1.49×, POD-512 1.26×) cannot be generated from the archive (no POD basis saved) and are quoted as external. Conclusions of §A11/§A13 unchanged — mechanism real, POD-LSPG better and cheaper at every rung — only the size of the solve penalty was overstated. Report and `summary.json` (1055 rows) regenerated; no job rerun.

