   282	## 12. Jobs, memory, GPU-hours, defer order
   283	
   284	```mermaid
   285	flowchart LR
   286	  D[DESIGN + Codex audit]:::doc --> C[code + Codex code audit]:::doc --> S[smoke job: 2D 1024², 3D 65³, reduced training set, every control]:::job
   287	  S --> R{{coordinator release, phase II}}:::gate
   288	  R --> T1[t2d256 tuning]:::job & T2[t2d1024 tuning]:::job & T3[t3d64 tuning]:::job
   289	  T1 & T2 & T3 --> F[offline CPU scoring + frozen selection + Codex audit]:::doc
   290	  F --> E1[e2d256 verdict]:::job & E2[e2d1024 verdict]:::job & E3[e3d64 verdict]:::job
   291	  E1 & E2 & E3 --> A[results audit, make_report.py, report audit]:::doc
   292	  classDef doc fill:#e5e7eb,stroke:#374151; classDef job fill:#dbeafe,stroke:#1d4ed8; classDef gate fill:#fde68a,stroke:#b45309;
   293	```
   294	
   295	- One job per directory under `jcp-hrb/<job>/`, ≤ 2 concurrent, account total ≤ 8 checked before each submit.
   296	- **Memory.** Snapshots on the host (f64): 2D $1024^2$ 57.9 GB, 3D 36.9 GB; streamed in column blocks to the device for
   297	  the Gram. Host memory request 200 GB for those two cells. Device: $\Phi$ (2D $1024^2$, r=384: 3.2 GB), ECSW
   298	  contribution matrix (≤ $96\cdot512\times32768$ f64 = 12.9 GB in 3D), the `none` arm's $J$ (2D $1024^2$, r=384:
   299	  3.2 GB). A100-80 GB suffices; H200 if the smoke's measured peak exceeds 60 GB.
   300	- **Estimate** (to be replaced by a smoke-derived certificate, speed3d `resources.py` pattern): smoke ≤ 1;
   301	  tuning 2D256 0.5, 2D1024 2.5, 3D64 2.5; verdict 1.0 + 1.5 + 1.5; total ≈ 10.5 GPU-h, × 1.25 contingency ≈ 13 GPU-h,
   302	  inside the 30 GPU-h cap. A job is submitted only if ledger-spent + certified projection ≤ 30.
   303	- **Defer order** (first dropped first): `none` arms at r ≥ 256 (diagnostic) → the 2D $256^2$ cell → the 3D r = 512
   304	  rank → common-solver runs of non-front configurations. Never dropped: the 2D $1024^2$ and 3D $65^3$ ECSW and Q-DEIM
   305	  grids with the native solver, their picks and the verdict jobs. Dropped items are reported as deferred.
   306	- Cluster space: the tuning job's $\Phi$ and HR data (≤ 5 GB per cell) stay in its job dir until the verdict job has
   307	  read them (sha256-checked), then both dirs are pulled and deleted.
