   672	
   673	A3 governs where it differs from A1, A2 and the sections above. Item numbers are audit 3's.
   674	
   675	**A3.1 (item 7) Validation-informed budget, both methods, symmetric.** Two categories only:
   676	(T) **training-only construction** — work that uses no development/validation case (ours: bank training, per-mesh
   677	tables; baseline: snapshots, POD, advection POD, Q-DEIM pivoting, ECSW training runs and NNLS); and (V) **all
   678	validation-informed work** — every run on a development/validation case whose outcome selected or qualified a
   679	configuration, certification included, on both sides (ours: combined `c2grid`, `c2fbgrid`, `c3desc*` rule selection
   680	and escalation, `c3grid`, and speed3d `g1–g3`, plus P1d/P1e where they qualify an imported X; baseline: Stage A,
   681	Stage B, anchors and certification, the generator probe's E0 runs, the extension). Whole-job GPU-hours are split by the
   682	in-job phase timers; where ours' logs do not separate phases the whole job counts as V (stated). **Equal budget** is
   683	declared iff baseline V ∈ [0.8, 1.25] × ours' V for that dimension; otherwise every pair label of that dimension carries
   684	"**unequal-budget, descriptive**" (overrun or shortfall alike). T is reported for both, never omitted. Equal allocation is
   685	never reported as equal expenditure.
