   881	## Amendment A6 (2026-10-18) — design audit 6 (`audits/codex-design-6.md`, NEEDS-RESTATEMENT, no WRONG) and the design-level consequences of code audit 1 (`audits/codex-code-1.md`, NOT READY)
   882	
   883	**A6.1 POD certificate, final form (audit 6 item 2; code audit item 13).** With the Gram eigenvalues $\lambda_i$ and the
   884	exact $\|S\|_F^2$: $\tau_r^2=(\|S\|_F^2-\sum_{i\le r}\lambda_i)/\|S\|_F^2$. A negative radicand within $-10^{-12}$
   885	(roundoff) is clipped to 0; a more negative one fails the certificate. If $\tau_r<10^{-6}$ (saturated) the rank passes
   886	iff $e_r\le10^{-6}$; otherwise iff $|e_r-\tau_r|\le0.01\tau_r+10^{-6}$. Orthonormality ≤ 1e-10 and finiteness are
   887	required. The wording "far below any E0 error" is withdrawn: saturation means "below the registered
   888	training-projection certification tolerance", nothing more. **One basis per cell:** the method-of-snapshots basis
   889	unless the randomised fallback certifies strictly more registered ranks; ranks that fail under the chosen basis are not
   890	constructible (this replaces A5.2's "both bases fail" rule, which would mix two bases' prefixes). Construction is
   891	enforced in code: a non-constructible rank, an uncertified p, or a DEIM solve with backward error > 1e-12 raises a
   892	recorded construction failure; nothing is used silently.
   893	
   894	**A6.2 Randomised fallback dimensions (audit 6 item 3).** Sketch $\ell=\min(q_{\max}+64,\,n_{\rm snapshots},\,
   895	n_{\rm spatial})$ with $q_{\max}=r_{\max}$ (state POD) or $p_{\max}$ (advection POD); a requested rank or p larger than
   896	the snapshot count is not constructible (no completion of the basis). A non-finite method-of-snapshots factor triggers
   897	the fallback before use.
   898	
   899	**A6.3 N-under ladder, restated (code audit item 9).** An under-sampled ECSW support below $r$ makes the LSPG problem
   900	underdetermined, so its solution is not unique and it cannot be Q1-qualified; such levels show solver/qualification
   901	failure, not "sampling-induced accuracy degradation". The ECSW ladder is therefore support caps
   902	$\{r,\lceil r/2\rceil,\lceil r/4\rceil,\lceil r/8\rceil\}$ (r points is already far below the registered τ supports),
   903	the Q-DEIM ladder $p\in\{\lfloor r/8\rfloor,\lfloor r/16\rfloor,\dots,1\}$ (each p certified by A6.1 on the advection
   904	POD). Every level is run on both fixtures with its own tight and tighter anchors (complete Q1). A family's control
   905	**fires** iff some level is Q1-qualified **and** its median E0 error on the fixtures ≥ 2 × the `none` arm's; Q1-failing
   906	levels are reported as solver failures. If no level fires the control is unfulfilled (A2.10 applies).
   907	
   908	**A6.4 Native solver for underdetermined Jacobians (code audit item 2).** The native Gauss–Newton step is the
   909	minimum-norm least-squares solution when the reduced residual has fewer rows than unknowns (QR of $J^\top$), and the
   910	Householder-QR solution otherwise; a non-finite step (rank deficiency) is exit reason 3.
   911	
   912	**A6.5 Validity includes damping saturation (code audit item 5).** A run is invalid if, at any live step, the LM damping
   913	is non-finite or at its limit $10^{14}$, independently of the exit reason.
   914	
   915	**A6.6 Timing estimands, exact (code audit items 6, 7, 8).** For a pair: per timing case, $v_c$ = median of that case's
   916	valid ratios; the statistic is $T=\mathrm{median}_c\,v_c$ over the six registered timing cases (numpy median: the
   917	mean of the two middle values); its 95 % interval and the 90 % interval of $\log T$ come from resampling cases (10,000,
   918	seed 0). A pair is assessed only if all six registered timing cases have ≥ 1 valid triple. Role selection uses the same
   919	$T$ with single warm runs (A4.8, A5.3). N-time runs on all six timing cases and passes iff $T\in[1.8,2.2]$ and the
   920	lower 95 % bound exceeds 1 ("X faster"). Every timed output is compared with its separately scored output (≤ 1e-12);
   921	every attempt (including rejected triples) is kept; screening runs are preceded by a 0.1 s burn.
   922	
   923	**A6.7 Acceptance is schema-driven (code audit item 3).** `smoke_accept.py` requires an explicit list of phases and
   924	gates per cell and recomputes each predicate from numbers (certificates from projection errors, Q1 from per-run
   925	evidence and from distances recomputed out of the saved fields, timing statistics from raw triples, G-score from saved
   926	coefficients); a missing, skipped, errored or non-finite required item fails; an unavailable fixture is "unfulfilled".
   927	The CPU gate file `checks/test_core.json` (all 13 gates) is a required input.
   928	
   929	**A6.8 Metadata pin (code audit item 17).** Jobs run with `JCPREF_META` unset; `score.check_store` asserts the loader's
   930	metadata directory is the lane's pinned `e0/store` and hashes the exact STATUS file the loader reads.
