  1174	## Amendment A16 (2026-10-18) — design audit 9 (`audits/codex-design-9.md`, NEEDS-RESTATEMENT, no WRONG)
  1175	
  1176	**A16.1 Name and claims.** The ECSW arm is "**ECSW with support-targeted greedy NNLS**": the Petrov–Galerkin ECSW
  1177	gradient-matching NNLS of Grimberg et al., sampled at support targets $\kappa r$ instead of stopped at a training-residual
  1178	tolerance (the published stopping rule). For every configuration the actual support, the training relative residual at
  1179	the checkpoint, construction failures and Q1 are reported. No claim that this grid guarantees a strong or unbiased
  1180	baseline is made.
  1181	
  1182	**A16.2 Migration of the extension and coverage rules.** A2.18: the ECSW boundary is κ = 8 and its single extension is
  1183	κ = 16 (replacing "smallest τ"). A3.11: ECSW coverage is reported per attempted/constructed (r, κ); a failed κ = 8 or
  1184	κ = 16 construction makes the cell's ECSW statements carry "ECSW coverage incomplete". The cap-retry rule of A1.8/A3.11
  1185	is withdrawn. **Continuation:** every greedy path is built through 16r from the start (checkpoints 2r, 4r, 8r, 16r; the
  1186	batch size depends only on the current support, so earlier checkpoints are identical to those of a shorter path except
  1187	for the final batch at the cap); the 16r checkpoint is used only when the extension rule triggers. Its construction
  1188	cost is in the resource certificate.
  1189	
  1190	**A16.3 Banning consequence.** If a target is unreached and more than 1 % of the candidates were banned, the path is
  1191	rebuilt once with banning disabled (iteration-bounded); the path reaching more targets is used, both are reported, and a
  1192	target still unreached is a construction failure (A16.2 coverage label). smk2 exercises this on the 3D case that failed
  1193	in smk1; if the retry is not triggered or does not help, that is reported.
  1194	
  1195	**A16.4 Accounting.** The development-case evidence used to choose the knob and the fixtures (smk1 and the CPU dry runs)
  1196	is validation-informed and counts in the baseline's V budget (A3.1). The discarded τ-knob evidence is retained in
  1197	`runs/smk1`. The amended grid (κ ∈ {2, 4, 8}; extension 16) is frozen before production.
  1198	
  1199	**A16.5 (design audit 10, code audit 12) Retry rule frozen.** The ban-free retry runs **whenever more than 1 % of the
  1200	candidates were banned** on the initial path (regardless of target attainment). Both paths use the same iteration bound
  1201	(20,000 NNLS iterations). One whole path is selected by a training-only order: more reached targets; then the smaller sum
  1202	of $\log_{10}$ training residuals over the targets both paths reached; then the initial path. Selection happens at
  1203	construction, before any validation run, and both attempts (diagnostics, checkpoint supports and weights) are kept and
  1204	reported; acceptance recomputes the trigger and the selection and counts supports from the saved weights. If the
  1205	selected path still banned more than 1 % of the candidates (only possible when the retry was not better), that rank's
  1206	ECSW statements carry "**ECSW construction quality limited (banning)**", blocking "adequately tuned ECSW" and exhaustive
  1207	non-domination wording for that cell.
