  1211	## Amendment A17 (2026-10-18) — NNLS algorithm, from the CPU dry run (training-only fixture, no verdict data)
  1212	
  1213	On a training-only fixture (2D L = 256, r = 16, the ECSW contribution matrix 1,920 × 32,768) the path to 16r = 256
  1214	needed 6,444 iterations and banned 7,563 candidates; a reference single-index Lawson–Hanson in numpy needed about 300.
  1215	Two causes: (i) the normal-equation refit (Cholesky of $G_S^\top G_S$) loses the positivity of a newly entered index to
  1216	round-off, and (ii) batch additions (2 % of the support) add correlated indices that the refit then drops, so they
  1217	re-enter and cycle. **A17.1:** every passive-set least-squares problem is solved on the original columns by Householder
  1218	QR on the device, and the gradient is recomputed exactly from the residual each iteration. **A17.2:** classic
  1219	single-index entry (batch fraction 0): on the fixture this reaches 128 points in 147 iterations with no bans, the same
  1220	path as the reference. The iteration bound becomes 40,000 (≈ 1.15 × the largest target at 3D r = 1,024 plus margin),
  1221	replacing A16.5's 20,000 for both attempts; the ban-free retry rule is otherwise unchanged. The cost of one path is
  1222	about $m\sum_k k^2$ flops for the QR solves (3D smoke r = 256: about $10^{15}$); for production ranks this is large
  1223	(3D r = 1,024: about $10^{17}$), so phase II will need an updating QR (append/delete columns, $O(mk)$ per step); this is
  1224	recorded as a phase-II implementation item with its own code audit, and the smoke measures the cost at r = 256.
  1225	
  1226	**A18 (2026-10-18) — design audit 12 and code audit 15 on A17.**
  1227	- **A18.1 Evidence.** Every NNLS attempt now returns, and the smoke saves, each checkpoint's residual vector, $\|b\|$
  1228	  and the per-candidate drop counters; acceptance recomputes checkpoint residuals and ban counts from them, and checks
  1229	  both KKT inequalities for any KKT-terminated pilot (in addition to the pilot's saved support, weights and residual).
  1230	- **A18.2 Rank-deficient passive sets.** The passive-set least squares uses Householder QR on the original columns; if
  1231	  the support has more columns than rows or $\min_i|R_{ii}|\le10^{-13}\max_i|R_{ii}|$, the minimum-norm SVD least
  1232	  squares (A7.2) is used. Column padding (for compilation) never exceeds the row count.
  1233	- **A18.3 Corrections to A17.** The iteration bound is 40,000 outer iterations (one entry attempt and its full
  1234	  Lawson–Hanson refit per iteration) for each attempt, about 2.44 × the largest support target (16 × 1,024); the "1.15 ×"
  1235	  statement was wrong. The dry-run comparison was at different endpoints: the old algorithm needed 6,444 iterations for
  1236	  256 points, the repaired one 147 iterations for 128 points with no bans, the same trajectory as a numpy reference at
  1237	  the checkpoints compared; the two mechanisms in A17 are diagnoses, consistent with but not isolated by these runs. The
  1238	  fixture record (scripts and logs) is archived in `runs/nnls_fixture/`. All four checkpoints (2r, 4r, 8r, 16r), both
  1239	  saved attempts, the A16.5 selection order and the coverage/banning labels stand; the batch-dependent caveat of A16.2
  1240	  is retired (single-index entry).
  1241	- **A18.4** Path diagnostics pair each support size with the residual of the same iterate.
  1242	- **A18.5 Feasibility.** Repeated full QR is cubic in the attained support; the smoke measures its cost at the smoke
  1243	  ranks only. Before phase II, an updating QR (append/delete with periodic refactorisation and gradient refresh, its
  1244	  tolerances frozen and its checkpoints compared with the full-QR path on the smoke fixtures) or a reduced production
  1245	  scope is registered, and the resource certificate is regenerated for the final algorithm including the 16r
  1246	  continuation and the retry. The 30 GPU-h cap and the incomplete-coverage labels stand.
  1247	
  1248	**A18.6 (code audit 16, design audit 13).** A18.1's persistence applies to the **support checkpoints** (the registered
  1249	knob); tolerance crossings are reported as scalars only. The fixture archive `runs/nnls_fixture/` is completed by the
  1250	logs `t4.log`, `t7.log` and `G.sha256` (generated on the local CPU after A18; committed when present), and `t_old.py`

