  1356	every 256 appends (identical supports at every checkpoint, residuals to 1e-10) with drift ≤ 1e-8. In production, a
  1357	drift above 1e-8 at a refactorisation is a recorded **stability event**; any event makes that path's construction
  1358	"quality limited (orthogonality)" with the A16.5 consequences. Dependent-column skips, drift values, drift events,
  1359	interval and buffer capacity are persisted per attempt (`build.ecsw_weights`).
