  1383	## Amendment A24 (2026-10-18) — code audit 18 / design audit 16, cost model, phase-II job structure
  1384	
  1385	**A24.1 A23 wording and evidence.** "Solved exactly" is withdrawn: a path that stops early **satisfies the registered
  1386	numerical KKT certificate** (the solver's KKT flag, both gradient inequalities with tolerance $10^{-9}\|G\|_F\|b\|$,
  1387	and — from A24 on — finite non-negative terminal weights whose count equals the reported support and whose saved
  1388	residual vector reproduces the reported residual). The full-QR and updating-QR paths **agree on the binding regression
  1389	fixtures** (not universally). An optimum used as a target remains subject to Q1, support disclosure and the
  1390	construction-quality labels. The terminal support, weights and residual vector of every attempt are saved; smk2 predates
  1391	this and is accepted under the legacy rule with that provenance stated.
  1392	
  1393	**A24.2 Cost model (corrected).** One NNLS path to support s with m rows, N candidates, buffer width K: appends
  1394	$8mK$ flops each ($8mKs$ in all; memory traffic $32mKs$ bytes), gradient refreshes $2mN$ flops per iteration,
  1395	refactorisation at k columns ≈ $2mk^2$ (Householder) $+ 2mk^2$ (explicit Q) $+ 2mk^2$ (drift product) flops, every
  1396	1,024 appends. For 3D r = 1,024 (m = 104,448, N = 32,768, s = K = 16,384): appends ≈ 2.2e14 flops / 9.0e14 bytes,
  1397	gradients ≈ 1.2e14 flops (≈ 1.9e4 iterations) and 4.2e15 bytes (reading G each time), refactorisations
  1398	$\sum_{j\le16}6m(1024j)^2$ ≈ 9.8e14 flops; total ≈ 1.3e15 flops and ≈ 5e15 bytes (memory-bound: ≈ 20 min on an H200);
  1399	the retry rule can double it. Refactorisation still grows cubically in the attained support (A20.4's "no longer cubic"
  1400	is withdrawn); at these sizes it is not dominant.
  1401	
  1402	**A24.3 Construction-quality labels (code 18 item 2).** Each rank's ECSW construction carries a quality label:
  1403	"ok", "limited (orthogonality)" (any non-finite or > 1e-8 drift at a refactorisation), "limited (banning)" (> 1 % of the
  1404	candidates banned on the selected path), or both; the label is recomputed offline from the saved drift values and ban
  1405	counters and propagates to every ECSW configuration of that rank (A16.5 consequences).
  1406	
  1407	**A24.4 Phase-II jobs.** Per cell (2D 256², 2D 1024², 3D 65³) a **tuning job** (`tune.py`): offline construction from
  1408	training data, saturation (256² only), adequacy, generator probe (basis + `none`/native screening runs), Stage A with
  1409	in-job certification and anchors, ours' batch-1 replay and same-job warm timing on the 6 timing cases, and the
  1410	full-rank limiting comparator on the verdict cohort. Its artifacts (Φ, per-configuration HR data, ECSW paths) stay in
  1411	the job directory for the next job. After offline Stage-B freezing (A2.6, A5.3) and a regenerated certificate, a
  1412	**Stage-B job** per cell runs the frozen Stage-B members on the full verdict cohort with Q1, and the A–B–A timing of
  1413	every (X, B) pair admitted by A1.12 on the 6 timing cases; picks and labels are then computed offline from that job's
  1414	data (A1.6) and frozen with sha256 before the report. Memory admission (A22.2): the 3D tuning job records the device
  1415	peak before and after the r = 1,024 ECSW path (JAX reports the process-cumulative peak, so the path's own peak is
  1416	known only when it sets a new one); a new peak > 120 GB (decimal) makes that rank "not constructible (memory)".
  1417	
  1418	**A24.5 G-ours inputs.** 2D: the per-case E0 of each batch-1 key from jcp-p1-scaling `checks/analysis.json`
  1419	(`inputs/p1_analysis.json`, keys `dev6|0..5`). 3D: the per-case E0 of each batch-1 key on the selection cohort
  1420	(seed 923801, cases 0–5) extracted from speed3d `checks/scores-g{1,2,3}.json` at commit 691465d88 into
  1421	`inputs/speed3d_batch1_e0.json` (source sha256 recorded). Ours' 3D settings (bank, R', adaptive start a) are speed3d
  1422	`configs/r1.json`'s: M2_512 = (M2, 512, 3), W256/W512/W768/W1024 = (W1024, R', 6). G-ours is evaluated in the tuning
  1423	job (screening cases = timing cases) and again in the Stage-B job; a failure in either removes that X (reported).
