  1457	## Amendment A26 (2026-10-18) — design audit 17 (WRONG) and code audit 19 (NOT READY)
  1458	
  1459	**A26.1 NNLS cost and memory admission (design 17 items 2, 4; code 19 items 4, 14).** A24.2's gradient traffic is
  1460	corrected: reading $G$ ($8mN$ bytes) on each of $I$ iterations is $8mNI \approx 5.2\times10^{14}$ bytes for the
  1461	**assumed** $I = 19{,}000$ (the bound is 40,000 per attempt), not $4.2\times10^{15}$; appends plus gradient reads total
  1462	≈ $1.42\times10^{15}$ bytes (≈ 5 min at the H200's 4.8 TB/s peak; the projection uses an effective 2 TB/s, ≈ 12 min,
  1463	doubled for the A16.5 retry). Refactorisations are ≈ 73 % of the listed flops; deletions, residual formation, triangular
  1464	solves, compilation and refactor temporaries are not in the arithmetic and are measured in-job (phase timers). Nothing
  1465	in this arithmetic is a certificate (A26.4). Memory admission (replaces A24.4's rule): after the 3D r = 1,024 path the
  1466	**process-cumulative** device peak must be finite and ≤ 120 GB (decimal); a higher or missing value — whatever phase
  1467	caused it — makes that rank's ECSW "not constructible (memory)"; an out-of-memory error during the path does the same
  1468	(the phase fails, its error is recorded). The path is built after basis, advection POD and the probe basis, before any
  1469	Q-DEIM construction.
  1470	
  1471	**A26.2 Evidence integrity (code 19 items 2, 3, 10, 11, 12).** (a) Offline optimum acceptance requires the saved
  1472	terminal solution (unique in-mesh integer nodes, finite strictly positive weights, count = final support, residual
  1473	vector reproducing the final residual) and that every optimum checkpoint equals it (alias); terminal arrays may be
  1474	absent only for the pinned legacy attempt smk2 (`smoke_accept.LEGACY_NO_TERMINAL`, by attempt name). (b) The ECSW
  1475	construction-quality label is stored on every ECSW configuration and is required for post-A24 attempts. (c) The tuning
  1476	job predeclares the registered inventory (every rank × HR knob × option × solver) with statuses not_run /
  1477	construction_failed / run_failed / complete / deferred, checkpoints each configuration and each comparator case as it
  1478	completes, and isolates failures per solver, per comparator and per FOM case. (d) A configuration whose warm timed
  1479	output differs from its scored output (non-finite or > 1e-12) is `timing_ok = false` and never enters an absolute-time
  1480	or X-specific front; ours' timed output is compared with its preceding (scored) call the same way. (e) Every full-rank
  1481	limiting-comparator solve is checked for convergence (finite residuals ≤ the Newton tolerance on every step); a failed
  1482	solve is a failed entry, and the full E0 record is kept.
  1483	
  1484	**A26.3 Registered consequences implemented (code 19 items 6, 7).** Saturation (A1.3) runs before adequacy; if it fails
  1485	at any registered rank, the all-step POD (certified on all states) replaces the 256² basis (with its trust radii and
  1486	constructible set) before any downstream construction, and the 1024² cell is labelled "snapshot-limited". Adequacy
  1487	(A2.2) uses the first 32 trajectories of the seeded permutation (seed 20261017) on the basis actually used. Generator
  1488	probe runs are made only at ranks the probe basis certifies; other ranks are "construction_failed"; per-case E0 records
  1489	and output coefficients are kept. Order of the tuning job: comparators (ours, G-ours) → construction → the HR grids
  1490	(never deferred) → `none` at r < 256 → full-rank limiting comparator → deferrable work in the registered defer order
  1491	(`none` at r ≥ 256, then the extension, then the probe runs), started only while elapsed < 0.85 × the job budget;
  1492	deferred items are listed as such.
  1493	
  1494	**A26.4 Resource certificate restated (code 19 item 15; design 17 item 6).** The per-item projections of A25.3 are
  1495	conditional models, not a certificate, and are relabelled "projected". The certificate is the hard bound: a 1-GPU job
  1496	cannot spend more than its Slurm wall limit. Wall limits: tuning 2D 256² 2 h, 2D 1024² 5 h, 3D 65³ 12 h (budget for
  1497	deferrable work = wall − 0.25 h); Stage-B reserve 7.5 h; spent 1.512 → bound 28.0 ≤ 30 GPU-h. If a tuning job is
  1498	truncated by its limit, the unfinished configurations remain `not_run` and the cell's coverage statement says so. The
  1499	Stage-B jobs' limits are set from the frozen Stage-B inventory and the tuning job's measured per-configuration times,
  1500	inside the reserve (re-certified before submission).
  1501	
  1502	**A26.5 Stage B and picks (design 17 item 4).** A24.4 supersedes §6/A21.3's "picks frozen before the verdict job":
  1503	Stage-B **membership** is frozen (sha256, audited) before the Stage-B job; picks are computed afterwards from that job's
  1504	full-cohort data (A1.6) and frozen before the report. To cover every possible role candidate, the Stage-B job A–B–A
  1505	times **every** Stage-B member that is Q1-qualified on the verdict cohort against **every** admitted X (G-ours passed in
  1506	both jobs), not only A1.12's exploratory envelope-filtered set.
  1507	
